# {{name}}

A game built on [Crucible](https://github.com/kryptic-sh/crcbl).

```sh
crcbl run                  # open a window
crcbl run --headless       # no window; what CI runs
crcbl build --release
```

`crcbl run --headless` is not a lesser mode: it is the same loop with
`HeadlessShell` in place of a window system, so a determinism check or a
regression test needs no display and no GPU. `.github/workflows/ci.yml` runs it
on every push.

## Layout

| Path | What |
| --- | --- |
| `src/main.rs` | The engine loop: pump events, tick at a fixed rate, present. |
| `scenes/` | Scene files. The format lands with `crcbl-scene`; the directory is here so the path is stable. |

## The engine dependency

`Cargo.toml` points at a Crucible checkout by path, because the engine is not
published yet. Moving this project without moving the engine breaks the build;
fix it by editing that one path, or re-run `crcbl new --engine <checkout>`.
